{{!-- Loot Shelf's shelf-Buy control pointed the other way (see loot-take.hbs there).
      `always-interactive` mirrors it and is required, not decorative: on a sheet the
      viewer can't edit, the framework disables every control without the class. What the
      button does is re-validated in the click handler (own the group and a member), so
      the class grants an affordance, never a permission. --}}
<div class="item-detail item-partystashTake" data-column-id="partystashTake">
    <button type="button" class="partystash-take-button always-interactive"
            aria-label="Take {{ item.name }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding" inert></i>
        <span>Take</span>
    </button>
</div>
